on/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Instruction codes is covered under “Basic Computer Organization and Design”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Computer registers, Computer instructions, Timing and Control, Instruction cycle, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Computer registers; Computer instructions; Timing and Control; Instruction cycle. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Organization problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** An interface defines a contract of operations that an implementation provides, helping separate caller expectations from implementation details.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Asynchronous Data Transfer; Modes Of Transfer; Priority Interrupt; DMA. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Organization problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Memory Hierarchy is covered under “Memory Organization”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Main Memory, Auxiliary Memory, Associative Memory, Cache Memory, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Main Memory; Auxiliary Memory; Associative Memory; Cache Memory. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Organization problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

