INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4400093534050125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Introduction to Linux in the context of Linux. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Operating System overview in the context of Operating System. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Process in the context of Process Management. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Scheduling -Basic Concept in the context of CPU Scheduling and Deadlocks. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to Linux is covered under “Linux”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Linux installation, Editing files with vi, vim, gcc, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Linux installation; Editing files with vi; vim; gcc. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Operating System problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** An operating system manages processes, memory, storage, I/O devices and protection while providing services to applications.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Operating System concepts; Functions of OS; Services of OS; System call. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Operating System problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Process is covered under “Process Management”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Process States, Process Control Block, Threads, User Level and Kernel level thread, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Process States; Process Control Block; Threads; User Level and Kernel level thread. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Operating System problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** The CPU executes program instructions and coordinates processing. Its major elements commonly include a control unit, arithmetic/logic unit and registers.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Preemptive and Non-Preemptive scheduling; scheduling criteria; Types of Scheduling algorithm: Non-Preemptive-First Come First Served (FCFS); Non-Preemptive- Shortest Job First (SJF). State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Operating System problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

