-- Software Engineering | ESE | easy | 4400093534020125
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4400093534020125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Software engineering in the context of Introduction to Software Engineering. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Metrics: The Management Spectrum 4P’s (People in the context of Project Management Concepts, Requirement Engineering &. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Software Scope in the context of Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Reactive versus Proactive Risk Strategies in the context of Risk Analysis And Management. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Software engineering applies systematic methods to software requirements, design, implementation, testing, deployment and maintenance, balancing quality, cost and time.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Dual role of software; Various Myths Associated with Software; Different Software Process Models; The Linear Sequential Model. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Metrics: The Management Spectrum 4P’s (People is covered under “Project Management Concepts, Requirement Engineering &”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Project, Product and Process), The W5HH Principle, Basic concept of Requirement (Functional & Non Functional), give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Project; Product and Process); The W5HH Principle; Basic concept of Requirement (Functional & Non Functional). State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Software Scope is covered under “Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Feasibility Analysis, Empirical Estimation Models, Gantt Charts and Tools used, Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Feasibility Analysis; Empirical Estimation Models; Gantt Charts and Tools used; Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Reactive versus Proactive Risk Strategies is covered under “Risk Analysis And Management”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Risk Management Process, Risk Identification, Risk Projection, Risk Refinement, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Risk Management Process; Risk Identification; Risk Projection; Risk Refinement. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

