VALUES (4400093534020135, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Software engineering in Software Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Software Scope in Software Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Outcome of Design Process in Software Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Coding standards & Coding Guidelines in Software Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Software engineering applies systematic methods to software requirements, design, implementation, testing, deployment and maintenance, balancing quality, cost and time.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Dual role of software; Various Myths Associated with Software; Different Software Process Models; The Linear Sequential Model. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Software Scope is covered under “Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Feasibility Analysis, Empirical Estimation Models, Gantt Charts and Tools used, Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Feasibility Analysis; Empirical Estimation Models; Gantt Charts and Tools used; Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** UML provides standardized diagrams for modelling aspects of a software system. A use-case diagram shows actors and the services they interact with, not internal algorithms.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Effective Modular Design(Functional & Non-Functional); Cohesion; Coupling; Design and Modelling using UML. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Coding standards & Coding Guidelines is covered under “Software Coding & Testing”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Code Review, Software Documentation: Internal and External Documentation, Software Testing Fundamentals, Software Testing Techniques, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Code Review; Software Documentation: Internal and External Documentation; Software Testing Fundamentals; Software Testing Techniques. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

